      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The answer is straightforward and directly covered in [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never loading it there in the first place.** Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of spawned child processes** (the Ingest or Query agents) immediately before those processes start\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, an attacker cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables \u2014 the key exists only within the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5158,
      "output_tokens": 179
    }
